      "writtenOn": "2017-02-25T01:50:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It seems like this makes it harder to evolve the HAL.\n\nSuppose that we later want to extend the number of buckets to 32. If we constrain this type to uint16_t, then extending to 32 buckets would require a major version bump, no?\n\nIf we stick with uint32_t, then we could accommodate 32 buckets with a smaller API change (just changing the MAX_BUCKETS value).\n\nOr maybe I\u0027m misunderstanding the HIDL model?",
      "parentUuid": "64bfd358_3b68854f",
      "revId": "50c1f66802f32bc1a3c4a4d1334a578799ab4e30",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
